WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.150
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Tuesday, November 17.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.430
Here's what happened in transhumanism in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.830
Fast forward!

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.990
Anthropic says AI is speeding up AI research enough to trigger its safety rules.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.250
And a psychedelic eased depression by day two in a late-stage trial,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.680
with safety questions.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.420
Anthropic's Claude Mythos got new AMD chips running in about three days,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.940
a job that took months.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.910
Alibaba's new Qwen4-Max claims to rival top US models for far less.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.990
And scientists told OpenAI that AI nearly doubles their speed.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.470
Most expect discoveries years sooner.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.540
Meanwhile, OpenAI is letting outside safety teams inside,

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.110
to spot AI trying to dodge its controls.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.750
On to longevity. Centenarians' gut bugs tweak bile acids,

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.110
and boosting that in old mice improved metabolism.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.230
Closer to home, at Monash,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:14.300
mice without the protein granzyme K aged with healthier hearts and kidneys.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.950
And in old mice,

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:20.130
the heart's ageing signals cluster around its valves, not the muscle.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.550
And in an early trial, a heart gene therapy cut risky rhythms by 80%.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.250
On to wellbeing. In a small study,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.930
an ultrasound patch helped people reach dream sleep 43 minutes sooner.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.950
And a phone game called Fig helped people whose depression lingered on antidepressants,

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.230
though many dropped out.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.610
Now, the catch. Google found attackers using AI that turns security fixes into attacks,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.160
with no human involved.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.480
And Shanghai sacked two gene-editing researchers after a child's death,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.890
for not reporting safety findings in time.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.260
Voyager 1 is about to become the first hum

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.640
an-made thing a full light-day from Earth.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.220
NVIDIA says new software speeds a key step in

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.540
quantum error correction up to 13,000 times.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:21.260
Oh, and a Silicon Valley robot now reads the room partly through lab-grown human neurons,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.400
some in Australia.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.660
Relief in two days, new chips in three,

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.030
a hello a light-day out. Life's on fast forward.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.310
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.320
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
